WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.560
Welcome to this Seller University module on the generic product policy error codes 5886 and 5887.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.320
In this video, we'll explain what these error codes mean and how you can resolve them to successfully

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.920
list your products on Amazon.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:24.059
Error codes 5886 and 5887 indicate that you're trying to make changes to a product detail page that

00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:26.320
you're not authorized to modify.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:32.507
This could happen if you're trying to add offers to another seller's generic product or copy a product

00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:35.600
detail page to a store you're not approved for.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.440
You cannot directly edit or change a generic product detail page that belongs to another seller.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.720
If you want to sell a generic product, you need to create your own new product listing.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.680
To do this, you can use the add a product tool on Amazon Seller Central.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.720
This will allow you to create a new product detail page for the item you want to sell.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.349
Let's look at an example.

00:00:58.349 --> 00:01:01.280
Say you want to sell a generic smartphone case.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.160
You can't simply copy the detail page of an existing smartphone case listing.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.920
Instead, you need to create a new product detail page for your own smartphone case.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.080
This involves providing all the required product information, images and relevant details in the

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.840
add a product workflow.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:27.558
By creating your own new product, you'll be able to list and sell your generic items without running

00:01:27.558 --> 00:01:30.560
into the 5886 and 5887 error codes.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:37.236
More information on the Amazon generic product policy and related error codes can be found on the

00:01:37.236 --> 00:01:39.200
General Product Policy Help page.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.280
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
